# Public DNS resolvers benchmarked live (latency + failure rate).
# Schema per line:
#   <ip> <id> kind=dns owner=<owner> docs=<docs-url> tier=<default|optional> verified=<status>
# tier default = automatic benchmark pool (provider-grade anycast only).
# tier optional = regional/sanction-bypass/third-party: NEVER auto-selected,
#   used only with --dns-extra ID after a typed disclosure.
# verified=pending blocks use (see docs/DATA-REVIEW.md); only the maintainer
# flips it to verified after manual review. Never set it yourself.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
1.1.1.1 cloudflare kind=dns owner=Cloudflare docs=https://1.1.1.1 tier=default verified=true
8.8.8.8 google kind=dns owner=Google docs=https://developers.google.com/speed/public-dns tier=default verified=true
9.9.9.9 quad9 kind=dns owner=Quad9 docs=https://www.quad9.net tier=default verified=true
77.88.8.8 yandex kind=dns owner=Yandex docs=https://dns.yandex.com tier=optional verified=true
178.22.122.100 shecan kind=dns owner=Shecan docs=https://shecan.ir tier=optional verified=true
